# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# .env.local is gitignored by the default Vite template (matches the *.local
# pattern) — double check that after SPIKE-00, but never commit real values
# regardless.

# --- GitHub ---
# Create an empty repo on GitHub first (no README/license, so there's no
# merge conflict with the scaffolded project), then paste its URL here.
GITHUB_REPO_URL=<e.g. https://github.com/your-username/portfolio-os.git>

# Only needed for HTTPS pushes without an existing credential helper / SSH
# key already set up locally. Create one (classic token, "repo" scope is
# enough) at: https://github.com/settings/tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=<your-github-personal-access-token>

# --- Vercel ---
# Deployment now runs entirely through GitHub Actions (see
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml, from spikes.md SPIKE-01) — nothing local or
# agent-run ever calls Vercel directly, so credentials do NOT belong in this
# file. Instead, add them as GitHub Actions repository secrets:
#
#   Repo -> Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret
#
#   VERCEL_TOKEN        (from https://vercel.com/account/tokens)
#   VERCEL_ORG_ID        (from `vercel link`, run once locally, or from the
#   VERCEL_PROJECT_ID     Vercel project's Settings -> General page)
#
# `vercel link` requires an interactive login, so this is a one-time step
# only you can do — Claude Code will flag it and wait rather than guess.
